{"id": "currease30b_grpo_arms", "title": "Curriculum-Easy LR Sweep", "eyebrow": "Jupiter \u00b7 booster partition \u00b7 Qwen3-30B-A3B-Instruct-2507 \u00b7 GRPO", "subtitle": "Three learning-rate arms RL-training the same 30B MoE instruct model on real terminal-agent tasks in Daytona sandboxes, racing to step 50. How each arm is trending, what every metric means, and what actually happened to all those Slurm jobs.", "status_line": "3 arms alive \u2014 baseline 40/50, both sweep arms 20/50", "tiles": [{"hero": true, "label": "Task-completion reward \u00b7 baseline arm \u00b7 mean of its last 5 steps", "value": "0.32", "delta": "\u25ac flat after 40 of 50 steps \u2014 it was 0.37 over the first 5", "delta_tone": "flat", "detail": "binary pass/fail, 128 rollouts per step \u00b7 ~\u00b10.04 noise floor \u00b7 no arm has separated from another on reward"}, {"label": "Policy drift at step 20 (KL)", "value": "7\u00d7", "detail": "lr5e6 0.0177 vs lr1e6 0.0025 at the same step, in clean rank order \u2014 the LR lever is working even though reward has not moved"}, {"label": "Groups that produce gradient", "value": "26%", "detail": "baseline mean; the other 74% are all-8-wrong (54%) or all-8-right (20%) and give GRPO exactly zero signal"}, {"label": "Job relaunches survived", "value": "39", "detail": "ghost-GPU OOMs, EP backward hangs and bad resubmits \u2014 see the timeline below"}], "explainer": {"title": "What is this experiment?", "paragraphs": ["Unlike the GSM8K campaign that validated the stack, this one is a **research** run: the model is graded on whether it actually completes a terminal task \u2014 it drives a shell inside a Daytona sandbox under the Terminus-2 harness, and the reward is binary (task done / not done) on the `tasktrove_curriculum_easy_rl511` task set.", "All three arms are **identical except one lever**: the learning rate (1e-6 / 3e-6 / 5e-6). Same seed, same data, same 6 GH200 nodes, same 8 rollouts per task \u2014 so any daylight between the curves is caused by that one lever. The 3e-6 baseline arm started a day earlier and is correspondingly further along; compare arms **at equal step**, never at the right-hand edge.", "Read the reward curve with care. Each point is at most 128 binary rollouts, so its noise floor is around **\u00b10.04** even when nothing is changing, and step-to-step swings of 0.2 are routine. Forty steps in, the baseline is flat \u2014 0.37 across its first five steps, 0.32 across its last five. The honest current answer is *no separation yet on reward*, not *it works* and not *it fails*. The one place the learning rate visibly bites is KL drift."], "chips": ["model Qwen3-30B-A3B-Instruct-2507", "algo GRPO \u00b7 8 rollouts/task", "6 nodes/arm \u00b7 GH200", "FSDP2 + expert parallel", "128 samples/step", "target 50 steps", "KL coef 0.001 \u00b7 TIS cap 2.0", "seed 42 everywhere"]}, "step_target": 50, "charts": [{"field": "reward", "title": "Training reward by step", "big": true, "dp": 2, "y0": 0, "y1": 1, "yTicks": [0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1], "how": "Each line = the share of terminal tasks completed on that step's training batch. Up and to the right would be learning; 40 steps in, nothing here clears the noise floor. The two dips to exactly 0.00 are **not** collapses \u2014 they are thin-batch steps, see the last chart. Hover or focus + arrow keys for exact values."}, {"field": "entropy", "title": "Entropy \u2014 is anyone collapsing?", "dp": 3, "how": "Token-level hesitation. Drifting down = converging (fine). Crashing toward ~0.01 = mode collapse, the kill criterion. All three arms sit flat near 0.16 \u2014 nobody is collapsing."}, {"field": "kl", "title": "KL to reference \u2014 how far from base?", "dp": 4, "how": "Drift from the frozen starting model, held back by the KL penalty. **This is the one chart where the learning-rate lever is unmistakably working**: at step 20, lr5e6 has drifted about 7x further than lr1e6, in clean rank order. Reward has not followed."}, {"field": "len50", "title": "Answer length (median tokens)", "dp": 0, "how": "Median tokens per sampled answer. Watch for runaway growth (rambling) or a crash toward zero (degenerate short outputs). Steady in the 1,300\u20132,600 band throughout \u2014 neither pathology is present."}, {"field": "mixed", "title": "Mixed groups \u2014 is there signal left?", "dp": 2, "y0": 0, "y1": 1, "yTicks": [0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1], "how": "Share of tasks where the 8 rollouts disagree \u2014 the only place GRPO gradient comes from. Hovering near 0.25 means roughly three quarters of every batch is doing no work."}, {"field": "nsamp", "title": "Effective batch \u2014 how many samples actually counted", "dp": 0, "y0": 0, "how": "The nominal batch is 128 samples (16 tasks \u00d7 8 rollouts). The async trainer discards rollouts generated against a stale policy, and at the first step after a checkpoint resume that can cut almost everything \u2014 12 of the 13 post-resume steps ran short, twice down to a single group of 8. Read every dip on the reward chart against this line first."}], "glossary": "rl_default", "attempts": {"lr3e6": [{"v": "v1", "job": "1387081", "start": "04:15", "end": "09:13", "steps": "1-5", "fate": "hang", "note": "first attempt to survive a weight sync \u2014 the stack-validation milestone. EP/FSDP2 hang at s6 forward; jpbo-018 nodeset excluded"}, {"v": "v2", "job": "1388099", "start": "09:14", "end": "09:31", "steps": "-", "fate": "oom", "note": "ghost-OOM at checkpoint load (jpbo-019) while resuming from gs5"}, {"v": "v3", "job": "1388100", "start": "09:31", "end": "13:37", "steps": "6-10", "fate": "hang", "note": "resumed clean from gs5 on jpbo-122 \u2014 proving the ghost is per-node, not per-rack; hung after gs10"}, {"v": "v4", "job": "1389753", "start": "13:38", "end": "14:04", "steps": "-", "fate": "oom", "note": "ghost-OOM during bring-up"}, {"v": "v5", "job": "1389754", "start": "14:06", "end": "14:22", "steps": "-", "fate": "oom", "note": "ghost-OOM during bring-up"}, {"v": "v6", "job": "1389755", "start": "14:23", "end": "18:42", "steps": "11-15", "fate": "hang", "note": "banked gs15, then the backward hang again"}, {"v": "v7", "job": "1390982", "start": "18:43", "end": "19:09", "steps": "-", "fate": "oom", "note": "ghost-OOM during bring-up"}, {"v": "v8", "job": "1390983", "start": "19:53", "end": "23:21", "steps": "16-20", "fate": "hang", "note": "banked gs20 \u2014 the checkpoint the arm would spend the next day fighting back to"}, {"v": "v9", "job": "1392687", "start": "33:10", "end": "33:26", "steps": "-", "fate": "oom", "note": "ghost-OOM at resume load; machine-wide unclog left the pool ghost-heavy"}, {"v": "v10", "job": "1392688", "start": "36:41", "end": "36:55", "steps": "-", "fate": "oom", "note": "incident 38 \u2014 ghost-OOM at resume load on jpbo-107-[01-06]"}, {"v": "v11", "job": "1392689", "start": "36:56", "end": "36:57", "steps": "-", "fate": "fail", "note": "Slurm respawned the link onto the SAME dirty nodeset; scancelled as doomed before it could burn"}, {"v": "v12", "job": "1392690", "start": "36:58", "end": "37:12", "steps": "-", "fate": "oom", "note": "incident 38b \u2014 jpbo-076-38 GPU0 held ~82 GB of foreign residue, 29 MiB free; rack escalated to [01-48]"}, {"v": "v13", "job": "1392691", "start": "37:13", "end": "37:28", "steps": "-", "fate": "oom", "note": "incident 38c \u2014 third straight ghost-OOM, jpbo-026-41 (~84 GB residue); that rack escalated too"}, {"v": "v14", "job": "1392692", "start": "37:53", "end": "38:34", "steps": "21-22", "fate": "oom", "note": "incident 40 \u2014 cleared gs20 at last, then ghost-OOM in the backward peak on jpbo-040-24 (~62 GB residue)"}, {"v": "v15", "job": "1396944", "start": "38:36", "end": "38:37", "steps": "-", "fate": "fail", "note": "died in 9 s \u2014 rendered-sbatch resubmit from a shell without DCFT/proxy preamble; the WORKDIR guard exits 1"}, {"v": "v16", "job": "1396945", "start": "38:38", "end": "38:39", "steps": "-", "fate": "fail", "note": "same WORKDIR-guard exit, 8 s"}, {"v": "v17", "job": "1396946", "start": "38:40", "end": "38:41", "steps": "-", "fate": "fail", "note": "same WORKDIR-guard exit, 13 s \u2014 all three spares burned before the recipe was fixed"}, {"v": "v18", "job": "1397228", "start": "39:29", "end": "40:18", "steps": "21-22", "fate": "oom", "note": "incident 43 \u2014 ran clean 49 min, then ghost-OOM at gs22 backward on jpbo-074 (~60 GB residue appeared mid-run)"}, {"v": "v19", "job": "1397229", "start": "41:03", "end": "45:46", "steps": "21-25", "fate": "hang", "note": "finally banked gs25. Hung after it; 3h25m of dead nodes before the stall-watcher caught it"}, {"v": "v20", "job": "1397230", "start": "45:47", "end": "48:49", "steps": "26-30", "fate": "hang", "note": "resumed gs25, banked gs30, hung again \u2014 1h40m dead"}, {"v": "v21", "job": "1398002", "start": "48:50", "end": "54:34", "steps": "31-36", "fate": "hang", "note": "resumed gs30, banked gs35, hung \u2014 3h04m dead. Three consecutive hangs, one per checkpoint interval"}, {"v": "v22", "job": "1398003", "start": "54:35", "end": null, "steps": "36-40", "fate": "run", "note": "RUNNING on jpbo-057 \u2014 resumed gs35, now at 40/50, the furthest any arm has reached"}], "lr1e6": [{"v": "v1", "job": "1394803", "start": "36:41", "end": "36:52", "steps": "-", "fate": "oom", "note": "incident 37 \u2014 ghost-OOM at NCCL init on jpbo-076-[41-46], before a single step"}, {"v": "v2", "job": "1394804", "start": "36:53", "end": "42:33", "steps": "1-5", "fate": "hang", "note": "incident 47 \u2014 banked gs5, then backward hang exactly at the gs5 boundary (log and results froze in the same second); jpbo-081 rack-escalated"}, {"v": "v3", "job": "1394805", "start": "42:35", "end": "47:39", "steps": "6-10", "fate": "hang", "note": "resumed gs5, banked gs10, hung \u2014 3h10m of dead nodes before the scancel"}, {"v": "v4", "job": "1394806", "start": "47:40", "end": "52:52", "steps": "11-15", "fate": "hang", "note": "resumed gs10, banked gs15, hung \u2014 2h53m dead"}, {"v": "v5", "job": "1394807", "start": "52:53", "end": "57:15", "steps": "16-20", "fate": "hang", "note": "resumed gs15, banked gs20, hung \u2014 1h55m dead. Four hangs in a row, one per checkpoint interval, no OOMs"}, {"v": "v6", "job": "1394808", "start": "57:17", "end": null, "steps": "-", "fate": "run", "note": "RUNNING on jpbo-074-[03-09] \u2014 just started, resuming from gs20"}], "lr5e6": [{"v": "v0", "job": "1394836", "start": "36:41", "end": "37:54", "steps": "-", "fate": "fail", "note": "incident 39 \u2014 launched without the proxy preamble, so every Daytona call failed and every rollout scored a hard zero. 70 min of no-op steps; chain scancelled and the experiment dir wiped. Policy unharmed, data discarded \u2014 this arm's real history starts at v1"}, {"v": "v1", "job": "1396797", "start": "37:55", "end": "42:16", "steps": "1-5", "fate": "hang", "note": "incident 46 \u2014 relaunched with the proxy fixed, step 1 green (reward 0.50); EP/FSDP2 backward hang at gs5 on jpbo-051, confirmed frozen over a 13-min recheck"}, {"v": "v2", "job": "1396798", "start": "42:23", "end": "42:39", "steps": "-", "fate": "oom", "note": "incident 49 \u2014 ghost-OOM at init_model on jpbo-037 (~84 GB residue)"}, {"v": "v3", "job": "1396799", "start": "42:39", "end": "46:39", "steps": "6-10", "fate": "hang", "note": "resumed gs5, banked gs10, hung \u2014 2h26m dead"}, {"v": "v4", "job": "1396800", "start": "46:41", "end": "46:56", "steps": "-", "fate": "oom", "note": "ghost-OOM at init on jpbo-005 \u2014 the start of a nine-OOM night"}, {"v": "v5", "job": "1396801", "start": "46:58", "end": "47:57", "steps": "11-14", "fate": "oom", "note": "resumed gs10 and got four steps in before OOM on jpbo-015 \u2014 no new checkpoint, so all four were lost"}, {"v": "v6", "job": "1396802", "start": "47:58", "end": "48:14", "steps": "-", "fate": "oom", "note": "ghost-OOM at load (jpbo-027) \u2014 original chain exhausted"}, {"v": "v7", "job": "1400470", "start": "48:53", "end": "49:13", "steps": "-", "fate": "oom", "note": "fresh chain; ghost-OOM at load on jpbo-001"}, {"v": "v8", "job": "1400471", "start": "49:14", "end": "53:25", "steps": "11-15", "fate": "hang", "note": "re-did steps 11-15 and banked gs15 at last, then hung \u2014 2h07m dead"}, {"v": "v9", "job": "1400472", "start": "53:26", "end": "53:42", "steps": "-", "fate": "oom", "note": "ghost-OOM at load (jpbo-044)"}, {"v": "v10", "job": "1401107", "start": "53:43", "end": "53:59", "steps": "-", "fate": "oom", "note": "ghost-OOM at load (jpbo-042)"}, {"v": "v11", "job": "1401108", "start": "54:00", "end": "54:24", "steps": "-", "fate": "oom", "note": "ghost-OOM at load (jpbo-038) \u2014 third in 40 minutes"}, {"v": "v12", "job": "1401183", "start": "54:26", "end": "55:01", "steps": "16", "fate": "oom", "note": "resumed gs15, managed one step, OOM'd on the same jpbo-038 nodeset"}, {"v": "v13", "job": "1401184", "start": "55:03", "end": null, "steps": "16-20", "fate": "run", "note": "RUNNING on jpbo-038 \u2014 same nodes that killed v11 and v12, this time clean; back to 20/50"}]}, "timeline": {"title": "The job war \u2014 every Slurm attempt, Aug 16 04:00 \u2192 now", "how": "Each bar is one Slurm job; the dot at its end is how it died. Two enemies dominate. **Ghost-GPU OOM:** a node is returned to the pool before the previous job's GPU memory is actually released, so ours lands on a card already holding 60\u201385 GB of someone else's residue and dies at model load, checkpoint load, or the first backward peak. **EP/FSDP2 backward hang:** a known collective deadlock in expert-parallel backward. It cannot self-abort \u2014 blocking-wait mode is memory-load-bearing on 30B EP/FSDP2, so the NCCL watchdog is deliberately defanged and an external stall-watcher plus a human scancel is the detection layer. That is why every hang shows up in Slurm as CANCELLED rather than FAILED. The defense is the same either way: checkpoint every 5 steps, resume, exclude the crime scene, relaunch. Nothing but the steps since the last checkpoint was ever lost.", "t0": "04:00", "t1": "60:00", "tick_min": 240, "auto_now": true, "t0_date": "2026-08-16", "days": [{"at": "04:00", "label": "Sun Aug 16"}, {"at": "24:00", "label": "Mon Aug 17"}, {"at": "48:00", "label": "Tue Aug 18"}], "now": "57:31"}, "notes": [{"lead": "Provenance.", "text": "Metrics come from the trainer's own WandB runs, which log **offline** on Jupiter \u2014 one run per Slurm attempt, under each experiment dir. They are rsynced off the cluster and `wandb sync`ed into lukeleeai/jupiter-currease30b-grpo, then stitched per arm latest-attempt-wins per step. Nothing here updates on its own: every refresh is a manual sync (`scripts/dashboard/refresh_currease.sh`). Job IDs, nodes and windows are read from each attempt's wandb-metadata.json and from sacct; fates are cross-checked against the operator incident ledger and the driver logs."}, {"lead": "Thin batches at every resume.", "text": "The async trainer discards rollouts generated against a stale policy. At the first step after a checkpoint resume that bites hard: **12 of the 13 post-resume steps ran on less than the nominal 128 samples**, twice collapsing to a single group of 8. Both of the reward curve's dips to exactly 0.00 (lr1e6 step 16, lr5e6 step 11) are those 8-sample steps \u2014 one group of eight rollouts all failing, which is a coin-flip event, not a policy collapse. With 39 restarts behind these curves, a good share of the visible jitter is batch size, not learning. Check the effective-batch chart before reading anything into a spike."}, {"lead": "Reading the curves.", "text": "Reward is binary task completion averaged over the batch, so it is far noisier step-to-step than a math-accuracy curve \u2014 a single step's wobble means nothing. The metric to watch is **frac_groups_mixed**: only tasks where some of the 8 rollouts succeeded and some failed produce any gradient under GRPO. All-wrong and all-correct groups contribute exactly zero, and they remain about three quarters of every batch."}, {"lead": "Where the LR lever actually shows.", "text": "Reward is flat on all three arms, but **KL drift separates them cleanly and in rank order**: at step 20, lr1e6 sits at 0.0025 (essentially unmoved from the reference), lr3e6 at 0.0035, lr5e6 at 0.0177 \u2014 a 7x spread. lr5e6's entropy also runs slightly below the others. So the arms genuinely are different policies by now; that difference simply has not reached task completion. If reward is still flat at step 50 while KL keeps climbing, the honest read is that this task set is not teachable at this scale in 50 steps, not that the learning rate was wrong."}, {"lead": "What is not wrong.", "text": "Truncation is **zero** on every arm \u2014 no rollout is hitting the 32k context wall \u2014 the TIS importance ratio sits at 1.000, and no arm's entropy is collapsing. The gaps in grad-norm are async steps where a partial batch was discarded, the same events as the thin-batch chart."}], "series_meta": [{"key": "lr1e6", "name": "lr1e6", "label": "LR 1e-6 \u00b7 KL on", "color_slot": 1}, {"key": "lr3e6", "name": "lr3e6", "label": "LR 3e-6 \u00b7 baseline", "color_slot": 2}, {"key": "lr5e6", "name": "lr5e6", "label": "LR 5e-6 \u00b7 KL on", "color_slot": 3}], "series_data": {"lr1e6": [{"step": 1, "reward": 0.4453, "pass8": 0.5625, "entropy": 0.1687, "kl": 0.0024, "gradnorm": 0.6992, "clip": 0.0041, "mixed": 0.4375, "allwrong": 0.4375, "allcorrect": 0.125, "len50": 1428, "len90": 2563, "trunc": 0, "tis": 0.9996, "nsamp": 128, "discard": 0}, {"step": 2, "reward": 0.2656, "pass8": 0.3125, "entropy": 0.1637, "kl": 0.0027, "gradnorm": 0.2812, "clip": 0.0013, "mixed": 0.125, "allwrong": 0.6875, "allcorrect": 0.1875, "len50": 1499, "len90": 2472, "trunc": 0, "tis": 1.0002, "nsamp": 128, "discard": 0}, {"step": 3, "reward": 0.3984, "pass8": 0.5, "entropy": 0.1649, "kl": 0.0026, "gradnorm": 0.4517, "clip": 0.0021, "mixed": 0.25, "allwrong": 0.5, "allcorrect": 0.25, "len50": 188